<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>To Be Free | Feels Like Om</title>
    <meta name="description" content="To Be Free — a seven-day silent retreat in West Sikkim with Buddhist philosophy, meditation and four days of noble silence." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/type-system.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Feels Like Om</a>
      <nav class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary>ABOUT</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/about/our-story">Our story</a>
            <a href="/about/getting-to-sikkim">Getting to Sikkim</a>
            <a href="/about/visa-and-permits">Visa and permits</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary class="active">JOURNEYS</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/journeys/the-flagship">The Flagship</a>
            <a href="/journeys/how-to-embrace-suffering" aria-current="page">To Be Free</a>
            <a href="/journeys#feels-like-home">Feels Like Home</a>
            <a href="/journeys#way-of-the-yaks">Way of the Yaks</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a href="/reflections">REFLECTIONS</a>
        <a href="/contact">CONTACT</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="To Be Free page sections">
      <a href="#intentions"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Intentions</span></a>
      <a href="#who"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Who it’s for</span></a>
      <a href="#teacher"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Teacher</span></a>
      <a href="#journey"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Itinerary</span></a>
      <a href="#stay-longer"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Stay longer</span></a>
      <a href="#details"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Details</span></a>
      <a href="#faq"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">FAQ</span></a>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">West Sikkim | Silent retreat | Buddhist Philosophy</p>
          <h1>To Be Free</h1>
          <div class="hero-meta" aria-label="Retreat information">
            <p><strong>Group size:</strong> 2–6</p>
            <p><strong>Date:</strong> Nov 5-11 2026</p>
            <p><strong>Closing date:</strong> 1 October</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button hero-cta" href="/contact">Enquire about To Be Free →</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="opening-quote" aria-label="Opening reflection">
        <blockquote>
          “The answers to peace are all within us, otherwise we keep looking outwards.”
          <cite>— Tshampo</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </section>

      <section id="intentions" class="program-intro" aria-label="Retreat intentions">
        <div class="retreat-intro-inner">
          <div class="retreat-images" aria-label="Retreat image placeholders">
            <div class="image-placeholder retreat-image-large"><span>Meditation / monastery photograph</span></div>
            <div class="image-placeholder retreat-image-small"><span>West Sikkim photograph</span></div>
          </div>

          <div class="intent-copy intent-left">
            <p>This silent retreat is</p>
            <p>Less about what you can <em>gain</em></p>
            <p>More about what you can <em>let go of</em></p>
          </div>

          <div class="intent-copy intent-right">
            <p>You’re not a self-improvement project</p>
            <p>No “progress” to be measured</p>
            <p>Just slow down</p>
            <p>notice what’s going on</p>
            <p>within and around you</p>
            <p>then you decide</p>
            <p>what to let go of</p>
            <p>and how to go forward.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="intent-copy intent-center">
            <p>Embody the soul-expanding power of</p>
            <p>being alive,</p>
            <p>by being in the</p>
            <p class="present-word">present</p>
            <p>moment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="who" class="section who-section" aria-labelledby="who-title">
        <div class="wide">
          <h2 id="who-title">Who is this for?</h2>
          <div class="who-summary">
            <div class="who-summary-item">
              <svg class="who-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 32c6.8-10.4 14.8-15.6 24-15.6S49.2 21.6 56 32c-6.8 10.4-14.8 15.6-24 15.6S14.8 42.4 8 32Z" /><circle cx="32" cy="32" r="7.5" /></svg>
              <p>Curious, but apprehensive</p>
            </div>
            <div class="who-summary-item">
              <svg class="who-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 54V10h32v44" /><path d="M24 54V20h16v34" /><path d="M32 20v34" /></svg>
              <p>In a liminal period</p>
            </div>
            <div class="who-summary-item">
              <svg class="who-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="45" cy="17" r="7" /><path d="M7 50 24 27l10 12 7-8 16 19" /></svg>
              <p>Feeling called to meditate with Sikkim’s living energy</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="audience-grid">
            <article>
              <div class="audience-heading">
                <span>01</span>
                <svg class="audience-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 32c6.8-10.4 14.8-15.6 24-15.6S49.2 21.6 56 32c-6.8 10.4-14.8 15.6-24 15.6S14.8 42.4 8 32Z" /><circle cx="32" cy="32" r="7.5" /></svg>
                <h3>Curious, but apprehensive</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="audience-copy">
                <p>You’ve been curious about meditation, but the 10-day long silent retreats feel like a huge commitment.</p>
                <p>Ten days of no talking, no phone, just meditation. It can feel intimidating, especially for first timers.</p>
                <p>Part of you wants to try, but you might also be thinking “I’m not sure I can do that.”</p>
                <p>This retreat could be a stepping stone for you.</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article>
              <div class="audience-heading">
                <span>02</span>
                <svg class="audience-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 54V10h32v44" /><path d="M24 54V20h16v34" /><path d="M32 20v34" /></svg>
                <h3>In a liminal period</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="audience-copy">
                <p>“The word ‘liminal’ comes from the Latin word ‘limen’, which means threshold. To be in a liminal space means to be on the precipice of something new but not quite there yet.” <a href="https://www.verywellmind.com/the-impact-of-liminal-space-on-your-mental-health-5204371">Read more about liminal space here</a></p>
                <p>Maybe you feel stuck, experienced deep loss that made you confront impermanence, or consistently feel the ache of restlessness.</p>
                <p>Give yourself permission to step out of the container that can no longer contain who you might be becoming.</p>
                <p>Step into a space to slow down, explore who you are, and what you really want.</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article>
              <div class="audience-heading">
                <span>03</span>
                <svg class="audience-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="45" cy="17" r="7" /><path d="M7 50 24 27l10 12 7-8 16 19" /></svg>
                <h3>Feeling called to meditate with Sikkim’s living energy</h3>
              </div>
              <div class="audience-copy">
                <p>Every place has its own energy. People who have come here before say they felt a different kind of energy in Sikkim.</p>
                <p>According to Tibetan Buddhist tradition, Sikkim is considered a hidden land, a <em>beyul</em>, chosen and blessed by Guru Padmasambhava. It’s believed that meditating here multiples the merit, <em>for you and all beings.</em></p>
                <p>Walk among the trees. Talk to the river. Meditate with the mountains.</p>
                <p>Come and experience it for yourself, and decide what you feel.</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="teacher" class="teacher-section">
        <div class="teacher-media image-placeholder tall"><span>Portrait of Tshampo-la</span></div>
        <div class="teacher-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow dark">Your meditation teacher</p>
          <h2>Acharya Jigme Wongchuk Bhutia <span>(Tshampo-la)</span></h2>
          <blockquote>“Three years, three months, and three weeks.”</blockquote>
          <p>That’s how long Tshampo-la spent in intensive retreat.</p>
          <p>Despite understanding the Buddhist teachings on a deep theoretical level after twelve years of institutional training, he still felt something missing.</p>
          <p>So he entered silence for three years, three months, and three weeks.</p>
          <p>After the retreat, Tshampo-la understood that the inner peace we’re searching for is all within us. “Meditation makes me feel so free. The answers (to peace) are all within us, otherwise we keep looking outwards.”</p>
          <p class="teacher-pull">Book wisdom is so different from lived wisdom.</p>
          <p>Since the retreat, Tshampo-la has been teaching across Sikkim and internationally. He holds weekly meditation and Dharma talks for the villagers, teaches the young ones in monastic school, and has conducted Dharma teachings in Taiwan and Hong Kong.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="journey" class="section retreat-rhythm" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
        <div class="wide">
          <div class="journey-intro">
            <h2 id="journey-title">The seven-day journey</h2>
            <p>This residential retreat will be held entirely in English.</p>
            <h3 class="modes-title">Modes of learning</h3>
            <div class="modes-grid" aria-label="Modes of learning">
              <div class="mode-item"><svg class="mode-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 38c4-8 8-12 13-12s9 4 13 12"/><path d="M15 42h34"/><path d="M22 48h20"/></svg><p>Noble silence for four days</p></div>
              <div class="mode-item"><svg class="mode-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="32" cy="17" r="6"/><path d="M19 44c2-10 7-15 13-15s11 5 13 15"/><path d="M15 48h34"/></svg><p>Guided and silent meditation sessions</p></div>
              <div class="mode-item"><svg class="mode-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="20" cy="23" r="5"/><circle cx="32" cy="18" r="5"/><circle cx="44" cy="23" r="5"/><path d="M11 45c1-8 4-12 9-12s8 4 9 12"/><path d="M23 45c1-10 4-15 9-15s8 5 9 15"/><path d="M35 45c1-8 4-12 9-12s8 4 9 12"/></svg><p>Group discussions and reflections outside periods of noble silence</p></div>
              <div class="mode-item"><svg class="mode-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 17c8-3 14-2 20 2v30c-6-4-12-5-20-2V17Z"/><path d="M52 17c-8-3-14-2-20 2v30c6-4 12-5 20-2V17Z"/><path d="M32 19v30"/></svg><p>Daily Dharma talks with Tshampo-la</p></div>
              <div class="mode-item"><svg class="mode-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="21" cy="21" r="6"/><circle cx="43" cy="21" r="6"/><path d="M10 47c2-11 6-16 11-16s9 5 11 16"/><path d="M32 47c2-11 6-16 11-16s9 5 11 16"/><path d="M27 29h10"/></svg><p>Personalised 1-1 sessions with Tshampo-la</p></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="retreat-days">
            <article>
              <span>Day 1</span>
              <h3>Arrival and welcome</h3>
              <div class="day-detail"><p>Arrive at Bagdogra Airport</p><p>Private transportation to accommodation</p><p>Welcome dinner &amp; retreat orientation</p></div>
            </article>

            <article class="long-day">
              <div class="sticky-day-heading"><span>Days 2–5</span><h3>Being present in noble silence</h3></div>
              <div class="day-detail day-detail-long">
                <p>For four days, we enter noble silence.</p>
                <p>This means divorcing your phones and stepping away from ordinary conversations, so that your attention can be dedicated to your practice.</p>
                <p>A day may look like:</p>
                <ul><li>Morning meditation (sitting, then walking)</li><li>Breakfast</li><li>Dharma talk</li><li>Group meditation in monastery</li><li>Lunch</li><li>Rest / 1-1 sessions with Tshampo</li><li>Afternoon meditation</li><li>Dharma talk</li><li>Dinner</li><li>Metta meditation &amp; dedication</li></ul>
                <p>Tshampo-la said we always have to end the day with Metta meditation &amp; dedication.</p>
                <p>We dedicate the merits of our collecting practice to all beings:</p>
                <p><em>May I be free from suffering.</em><br /><em>May all beings be free from suffering.</em></p>
                <p>Themes covered include:</p>
                <ul><li>Introduction to Buddhist philosophy</li><li>Gratitude, a practice</li><li>Precious human life</li><li>Karma, everything is connected</li><li>Impermanence</li><li>Attachment</li><li>Ego and suffering</li></ul>
                <p>These themes supplement the meditation sessions.</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article><span>Day 6</span><h3>Gratitude and Metta Day</h3><div class="day-detail"><p>Tshampo-la has invited us to his village and to visit the monastery where he practises.</p><p>We will hold a gratitude and metta ceremony, to share the merits of our collective practice with all beings.</p><p>We’ll end the day with a closing dinner to celebrate the connections you’ve made over the past week.</p><p>And to celebrate you. 💗</p></div></article>
            <article><span>Day 7</span><h3>Not Goodbye</h3><div class="day-detail"><p>In Sikkim, instead of goodbye, we say <em>pheri bhetum</em>, may we meet again :-)</p><p>You may choose to depart or extend your stay.</p></div></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="stay-longer" class="section stay-longer"><div class="wide split-section"><div class="copy-block"><h2>Stay longer</h2><p>If you choose to extend your stay, there is an option to add on selected Feels Like Om field immersion activities.</p><p>Created with the intention of learning from nature and its people, these aren’t sightseeing activities, but immersive hands-on learning experiences.</p><p>We’re happy to speak with you if you’re interested. <a class="text-link" href="/journeys#feels-like-home">See a sample of our field immersion activities.</a></p></div><div class="image-stack"><div class="image-placeholder"><span>Field immersion photograph</span></div><div class="image-placeholder"><span>Community activity photograph</span></div></div></div></section>

      <section id="details" class="section details-section" aria-labelledby="details-title"><div class="wide"><h2 id="details-title">Details</h2><div class="details-grid"><article><h3>Retreat costs: SGD 500/person</h3><p>This covers your private-room accommodation, vegetarian meals, retreat logistics, and ceremony-related costs.</p><p>Airport transfers to and from Bagdogra are not included, but we can arrange them for you. Payment is made directly to your driver.</p><p>Flights, travel insurance, visas and permits, personal expenses, and optional field immersion activities are not included.</p></article><article><h3>Accommodation</h3><p>The retreat will be held at <strong>Ejam Residency</strong>, hosted by the Ejam family.</p><p>Every participant will have a private room with an attached bathroom and hot-water shower, giving you your own space to rest and be alone during the period of noble silence.</p></article><article><h3>Dana</h3><p>Tshampo-la offers the Dharma teachings and guided meditation sessions without a teaching fee.</p><p>If you wish, you may offer dana directly to Tshampo-la during the retreat.</p><p>Dana is entirely voluntary and only within your means.</p></article><article><h3>Supporting Feels Like Om</h3><p>There is no expectation to contribute beyond the retreat cost.</p><p>Feels Like Om is facilitating this retreat without taking any profits. All proceeds go towards supporting retreat costs.</p><p>We are working towards building a multi-generational third space in the village. A room where:</p><ul><li>Children can be children</li><li>Futures can be imagined and co-created</li><li>Small-scale collaborations in art, culture, music, science and learning can take place with and for the village community.</li></ul><p>If this is something you feel called to support, we’ll be very grateful.</p></article></div><div class="details-cta"><a class="button" href="/contact">Enquire about To Be Free →</a></div></div></section>

      <section id="faq" class="section faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="wide"><h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is this for Buddhists only?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. All you need is curiosity and a willingness to give yourself a chance. All backgrounds are welcome.</p><p>This retreat is grounded in Buddhist philosophy, but it is not about converting you to Buddhism.</p><p>Be curious. Be critical. Ask questions. Take what resonates with you, and leave the rest.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do I need meditation experience?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>No. First-time meditators and people with an existing practice are equally welcome.</p><p>Because the group size is kept intentionally small, there is time for questions, personal guidance, and one-to-one conversations with your teacher.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I need help during the period of Noble Silence?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Noble silence does not mean you cannot ask for help.</p><p>If you need emotional or meditation-related support, please speak with Tshampo-la.</p><p>If you need practical support, please look for a Feels Like Om facilitator or the homestay family.</p><p>Please always ask for help when you need it.</p></div></details><details><summary>How can I keep my loved ones updated?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>During the four days of noble silence, your devices will be safely kept for you.</p><p>We’ll provide you with a Singapore contact number that you can share with your loved ones. If there is an urgent need to reach you during the period of Noble Silence, they can contact us directly.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I can’t sit cross-legged for long periods?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Meditation is not a test of how long you can sit cross-legged. Chairs and other sitting arrangements can be made available if needed.</p><p>Let us know about any physical needs so we can work out what would be more comfortable and accessible for you.</p></div></details><details><summary>How do I get to Yuksom?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The nearest airport is Bagdogra Airport in West Bengal.</p><p>From there, the drive to Yuksom takes approximately six hours. We can help coordinate your transfer so you don’t have to arrange the journey on your own.</p><p>Before booking your flights, please speak with us.</p><p>We'll share recommended arrival and departure times so that your airport transfer and the drive can be planned comfortably.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/about/getting-to-sikkim"><strong>Read our guide to getting to Sikkim →</strong></a></p></div></details><details><summary>Do I need a visa or permit?</summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Depending on your nationality, you may need an Indian visa as well as the relevant permits to enter Sikkim.</p><p>We will guide you through the process before your trip.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/about/visa-and-permits"><strong>Read about visas and permits →</strong></a></p></div></details></div></div></section>

      <section class="section other-journeys"><div class="narrow center"><h2>Other journeys</h2></div></section>
    </main>

    <script>
      const sectionNav = document.querySelector('.section-nav');
      const hero = document.querySelector('.hero');
      const updateSectionNav = () => {
        if (!sectionNav || !hero) return;
        sectionNav.classList.toggle('is-visible', hero.getBoundingClientRect().bottom <= 0);
      };
      updateSectionNav();
      window.addEventListener('scroll', updateSectionNav, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', updateSectionNav);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
